      "name": "history-30-typed",
      "question": "Why?",
      "recognizedQuestion": "Why?",
      "answer": "Because a CUDA warp shares an instruction-issue mechanism across its 32 threads, rather than each thread issuing instructions independently. When threads take different branches, the GPU executes instructions with an active-lane mask so only the threads on that path participate. Modern GPUs support independent thread scheduling, but divergent paths still cannot execute as 32 completely independent instruction streams, so divergence can reduce efficiency.",
